# Relations this migration declares; probed by db-schema/tests/schema_fence.rs.
#
# This migration only widens seeded data, exactly as 0006 does, so there is
# nothing to declare: no relation, no column. `rows currency_kinds = N` is
# deliberately NOT used — it pins an exact count, and the currency roster is
# expected to grow, so that directive would turn every later seed widening into
# a failing assertion here.
#
# What pins the content instead is
# `the_instruments_view_derives_a_class_from_the_legs`, which registers QCAD-USD
# and asserts it derives `peg-pair`. That reads the class rather than the seed,
# so losing this row fails there as an `unclassified` derivation — which is the
# form the defect actually takes, since the liveness view picks its staleness
# bound by class.
none only widens the currency_kinds seed, creating no relation or column
